{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. Our system shows the second-floor printer (BL-PR-FL2) is offline for everyone, so the problem is with the printer itself rather than your laptop. Could you or someone near the printer please do the following? 1) Check the printer's screen for any error such as a paper jam, empty paper or toner, or an open door, and clear it if you can. 2) Turn the printer off for 30 seconds, then back on. 3) Make sure the network cable is firmly plugged in and the link light is on. Once that's done, reply here and let us know whether the printer's screen shows any error message and whether it came back online. If you need to print today, you can use another printer on a different floor; we can help you add it to your laptop. If the printer still shows offline after the power cycle with no error on screen, we will escalate it for a network or hardware check.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket EVAL-print-01, sender James O'Connor (user_id 8, Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, America/Chicago, usual hours 06:00-14:00). Account active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, VPN access enabled, one device BL-DT-0108. Checked check_device_status on BL-PR-FL2: online=false, last check-in 2026-10-10 21:59:50 UTC, no warnings, not assigned to a user. Per KB-022 this is a printer-side fault affecting all users, not a laptop issue (KB-023 not applicable). Did not perform the physical steps (screen error check, power cycle, cable/link light check); asked the user to do them. Next: if the printer is still offline after the power cycle with no on-screen error, re-run check_device_status and escalate to Tier 2 per KB-022 (possible network or hardware fault). Alternative printer via KB-024 offered to the user. Note: the printer's last check-in is about a day old relative to the ticket date, so it may have been down for some time; worth checking if others on the floor are affected.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-022",
    "KB-024"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
